From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 19:01:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03139/11362] [outer-loop] re-aim .418 remaining tasks at the
 REAL lever: solve MORE/DEEPER levels

The submission gate now measures the AUTHORITATIVE per-level metric (arc_agi.scorecard;
core_efficiency baseline 2.0074), and it shows the agent solves only 1 of 8 levels on
lp85. The score lever is REACHING DEEPER LEVELS, not trimming actions (every .417/.418
action-lever nulled; per the per-level metric the over-run doesn't even hurt the score).
Re-aimed the remaining .418 tasks off the (retired) action-trimming axis:

- A2 (exp4524) HEADLINE: was 'stop-after-levelup' (a wall-clock/harmful lever that caps
  levels) -> now REACH DEEPER LEVELS: diagnose + attack the L1->L2 barrier on a CORE game
  (deeper search / world-model DSL induction / energy-verifier next-level routing).
  Gate: a CORE game reaches L2 (core_efficiency > 2.0074) OR an actionable barrier
  diagnosis. Renamed deliverable -> experiment_4524_reach_deeper_levels.json.
- A4 (exp4526) integration: metric median-actions -> core_efficiency; wire only a lever
  that solved a deeper level.
- B1 (exp4527) infra: was 'promote nav diagnostics' -> harden the per-level efficiency
  gate (deepest-level + per-game efficiency first-class) AND fix the re-review MINOR:
  wire validate_canonical_baseline + an lp85 floor into --update-baseline.
- E (exp4531) capstone: 'navigation-efficiency scorecard' -> per-level efficiency
  scorecard (did core_efficiency rise / what is the L1->L2 barrier).

A3 (exp4525, the level-up-bank) unchanged (already the right axis). Level-up lint passes.
The gate fix held up: re-review verdict TRUSTWORTHY, all 3 CRITICALs resolved.

